WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.140
- If you only buy your paper products

00:00:02.140 --> 00:00:05.040
from Dunder Mifflin and
the gang at "The Office",

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:07.280
here are five other
titles worth checking out

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:09.080
on this week's "Binge Guide".

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:11.557
With eight of nine Fresh
seasons under its belt,

00:00:11.557 --> 00:00:13.550
"The Office" has cemented itself

00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:16.640
as one of the greatest
sitcoms of all time,

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:18.540
and is regaining popularity

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:20.450
with a new audience in the streaming age.

00:00:20.450 --> 00:00:22.960
And with trips to places
like a parks department,

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:25.680
a sheriff's department,
and an IT department,

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:28.050
this list will fill your "Office" void,

00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:29.827
starting with our Certified Fresh Pick,

00:00:29.827 --> 00:00:31.620
"Parks and Recreation".

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:34.880
Premiering back in 2009,
this mockumentary following

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:37.470
the inner workings of a parks
and recreation department,

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:41.480
ran for seven mostly Certified
Fresh seasons on NBC.

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:43.640
And one of the show's
creators, Michael Schur,

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:44.997
has also brought us comedies like

00:00:44.997 --> 00:00:47.320
"The Good Place" and "Brooklyn Nine-Nine",

00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:49.350
both of which you should also check out.

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:51.690
Critics call this one
of the very best sitcoms

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:54.430
on television, praising
it for finding fresh ways

00:00:54.430 --> 00:00:56.580
of utilizing its lovable ensemble

00:00:56.580 --> 00:00:58.760
and for being heartfelt yet hilarious

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:00.750
and snarky yet good-natured.

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:03.550
You can binge this show
in just under 46 hours,

00:01:03.550 --> 00:01:06.180
and don't forget the rest
of Michael Schur's comedies,

00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:09.940
which should fill up your binge
calendar until about 2022.

00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:14.040
Dialing in with our Editor's
Pick this week is "Reno 911!"

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:16.510
After six successful
seasons on Comedy Central

00:01:16.510 --> 00:01:19.600
starting back in 2003,
this improvised show

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:22.700
about inept officers in a
county sheriff's department

00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:26.040
returned this year for a
Fresh season run on Quibi.

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:28.427
The show, which also
spawned the 2007 film,

00:01:28.427 --> 00:01:32.060
"Reno 911!: Miami", has
been praised by critics

00:01:32.060 --> 00:01:35.110
for being an anarchically
hilarious ride along.

00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:37.710
You can binge all seven
seasons and the movie

00:01:37.710 --> 00:01:39.790
in about 36 and a half hours.

00:01:39.790 --> 00:01:41.340
For our Throwback Pick this week,

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:45.210
we're heading back to 2012
for "The Mindy Project"

00:01:45.210 --> 00:01:46.810
With six Fresh seasons,

00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:49.080
three airing on Fox and three on Hulu,

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:51.210
this show is about a young OB/GYN

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:54.140
trying to balance her
professional and personal life

00:01:54.140 --> 00:01:56.210
and trying to match the fairytale endings

00:01:56.210 --> 00:01:58.080
of her favorite romantic comedies.

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:00.300
After kick-starting her
career on "The Office",

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:03.410
star and creator Mindy Kaling
shines in what critics call

00:02:03.410 --> 00:02:06.160
a charming comedy, where
she earns consistent laughs

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:09.010
with her wit, charm, and physical comedy.

00:02:09.010 --> 00:02:11.160
It'll take you about 54 and a half hours

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:14.480
to binge all six seasons,
and you will eventually learn

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:17.650
that real life is nothing
like a romantic comedy.

00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:20.030
Remotely accessing our
Audience Pick this week

00:02:20.030 --> 00:02:22.090
is "The IT Crowd".

00:02:22.090 --> 00:02:25.720
This British comedy ran for
four seasons starting in 2006,

00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:27.330
and it's about the humorous adventures

00:02:27.330 --> 00:02:31.110
of a ragtag team of IT
workers at a huge corporation

00:02:31.110 --> 00:02:33.240
that's headed by a temperamental yuppie.

00:02:33.240 --> 00:02:34.310
Critics say that this show,

00:02:34.310 --> 00:02:36.440
which helped launch the
career of Chris O'Dowd,

00:02:36.440 --> 00:02:40.190
is a brainy riot that is
consistently funny and inventive.

00:02:40.190 --> 00:02:43.450
You can binge this one in just
about 10 and a half hours,

00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:45.510
but if you do it on your work computer,

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:47.770
you actually might hear from IT.

00:02:47.770 --> 00:02:51.590
And, finally, our Brand-New
Pick this week is "Superstore".

00:02:51.590 --> 00:02:54.710
This NBC workplace comedy
with five Fresh seasons,

00:02:54.710 --> 00:02:56.160
and a brand-new sixth season,

00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:58.680
follows employees working
at a big box store

00:02:58.680 --> 00:03:00.030
while taking a comedic approach

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:01.910
to timely, more heavy issues.

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:03.320
With a charming cast led by

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:05.510
the Emmy-winning America Ferrera,

00:03:05.510 --> 00:03:06.760
critics call "Superstore"

00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:09.750
one of the most lovable
ensembles on television.

00:03:09.750 --> 00:03:13.230
You can binge the first five
seasons in just over 37 hours,

00:03:13.230 --> 00:03:14.660
which is about the same amount of time

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:17.810
you need to walk every aisle
at your local superstore.

00:03:17.810 --> 00:03:19.640
Okay, hopefully this list will help

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:21.970
firm up your next few binge sessions.

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:23.240
That's what she said!

00:03:23.240 --> 00:03:25.470
Let us know what you're currently
streaming in the comments

00:03:25.470 --> 00:03:29.210
and be sure to check out the
new "Rotten Tomatoes is Wrong",

00:03:29.210 --> 00:03:32.350
a podcast from Rotten Tomatoes,
because Fresh and Rotten

00:03:32.350 --> 00:03:34.920
is just the beginning of the conversation.

00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:37.330
New episodes drop every Thursday,

00:03:37.330 --> 00:03:39.640
and you might be looking at
one of the hosts of the show.

00:03:39.640 --> 00:03:41.800
We'll see you back here
for more recommendations

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:43.300
based on the shows you love

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:45.384
on the Rotten Tomatoes' "Binge Guide"!

00:03:45.384 --> 00:03:47.884
(funky music)

